WEBVTT

00:05.751 --> 00:08.914
Oh! Brain freeze. Brain freeze.

00:09.288 --> 00:11.279
Hang in there, it'll pass.

00:11.456 --> 00:14.857
Going. Going. Going...

00:15.027 --> 00:17.427
okay, okay, I'm good.

00:19.097 --> 00:22.089
Oh! Brain freeze. Brain freeze.

00:22.501 --> 00:26.198
I don't think "brain freeze"
is an accurate description here.

00:27.940 --> 00:30.431
Oh, jeez. It's Mom.

00:31.310 --> 00:33.505
- Ah, great.
- Who's that she's with?

00:35.380 --> 00:37.439
I don't know.
They haven't been dating long.

00:37.616 --> 00:40.710
- How can you tell?
- He's still smiling.

00:40.886 --> 00:44.481
- Let's get out of here before she sees us.
- How? They're standing in the door.

00:44.656 --> 00:46.624
We'll go out the back.

00:46.825 --> 00:48.793
Hey, look. I'm a rabid dog.

00:53.332 --> 00:55.300
- Ah, damn it.
- Plan B?

00:56.568 --> 00:58.263
- Bathroom.
But I don't have to pee.

00:58.437 --> 00:59.631
Go! Go!

01:03.575 --> 01:05.509
Now what? We just wait here
till they leave?

01:05.677 --> 01:09.579
Would you rather go out there
and chat with Mom and her new boyfriend?

01:11.717 --> 01:14.550
Hey, Evelyn, get me a muffin too.

01:15.053 --> 01:16.213
Whoo!

01:16.388 --> 01:18.720
Somebody was drinking
more than coffee.

01:24.196 --> 01:25.424
Gonna be long?

01:25.597 --> 01:27.155
I don't know.

01:42.581 --> 01:45.414
&lt;i>And Bingo was his name-o&lt;/i>

01:49.655 --> 01:51.885
- All yours.
- Thanks.

02:11.543 --> 02:12.942
Thanks.

02:19.051 --> 02:21.986
So listen, when you guys
are done screwing around in here...

02:22.154 --> 02:24.418
...your mother would like to talk to you.

02:29.161 --> 02:31.220
Can I come out now?

03:00.058 --> 03:02.458
Hey, look who's here.

03:02.627 --> 03:03.651
It's Mom. Hi, Mom.

03:03.829 --> 03:05.319
Oh, stop it, both of you.

03:05.497 --> 03:08.398
I can't believe I'm such a horrible person,
you have to hide from me.

03:08.567 --> 03:11.968
- We werert hiding.
- Which does not invalidate your premise.

03:13.472 --> 03:15.736
Uh, Jake had, uh, stomach problems.

03:15.907 --> 03:18.137
Don't put this on me.

03:19.444 --> 03:21.412
I apologize for my children.

03:21.580 --> 03:23.571
No problem. Teddy Leopold.

03:23.749 --> 03:26.616
Oh, hi. Uh, Alan.
This is my brother, Charlie. My son, Jake.

03:26.785 --> 03:27.809
How you doing?

03:28.286 --> 03:31.016
Evelyrs told me a lot of wonderful things
about you boys.

03:33.759 --> 03:35.659
Not buying it, huh?

03:37.329 --> 03:38.796
I tried.

03:38.964 --> 03:41.933
Teddy lives in Denver,
but he does a lot of business in L. A...

03:42.100 --> 03:44.694
...so I helped him find a pied-à-terre
in Century City.

03:44.970 --> 03:46.198
What's a pied-à-terre?

03:46.638 --> 03:50.574
It's French for a place
to play hanky-panky with Grandma.

03:51.009 --> 03:52.237
- Mom!
- Mom!

03:52.611 --> 03:55.273
Oh, relax, it's not gonna scar him.

03:55.447 --> 03:57.779
Yeah, but what about us?

03:58.483 --> 03:59.950
Well, it was nice meeting you.

04:00.118 --> 04:03.610
- We've gotta bring the kid to his mother's.
- Again you're putting it on me?

04:05.023 --> 04:06.217
Nice to meet you too.

04:06.491 --> 04:07.822
Yeah, bye-bye. See you, Mom.

04:07.993 --> 04:09.426
- Bye, Mom.
- Bye.

04:10.896 --> 04:12.124
Wait, I have to pee.

04:12.297 --> 04:14.356
You've peed enough.

04:24.609 --> 04:27.305
Teddy Leopold.
Do we know a Teddy Leopold?

04:27.479 --> 04:28.844
It's Mom's new boyfriend.

04:29.014 --> 04:30.572
Oh, right, of course.

04:34.386 --> 04:37.878
- Arert you curious why he's calling?
- Not particularly.

04:38.056 --> 04:39.785
What if something happened to Mom?

04:40.192 --> 04:43.218
Then we'll just wait for Dorothy
to bring us the broom.

04:44.162 --> 04:45.925
Give me the phone.

04:49.034 --> 04:50.558
Hello?

04:50.735 --> 04:54.171
Uh, no, no, this is Alan.
Hi, Teddy. What's up?

04:54.339 --> 04:55.328
Uh-huh.

04:56.007 --> 04:56.996
Oh...

04:57.442 --> 04:58.636
Wow. Heh.

04:58.810 --> 05:00.675
That is quite an offer.

05:00.846 --> 05:02.746
L... I'd love to.

05:02.914 --> 05:04.313
Hang on, I'll ask him.

05:04.749 --> 05:07.650
- Teddy has invited us...
- I'm busy.

05:07.886 --> 05:10.616
- You at least wanna hear what it is?
- Nope.

05:12.257 --> 05:14.748
Charlie can't make it,
but can you still take me?

05:14.926 --> 05:17.520
Really? Heh-heh. Gee, thanks.

05:17.696 --> 05:19.425
I'll, uh... Guess I'll see you then.

05:27.505 --> 05:29.803
You're gonna be sorry.

05:30.809 --> 05:33.607
You're gonna be homeless.

05:34.246 --> 05:36.271
Why do you always have to play
that card?

05:36.548 --> 05:40.450
&lt;i>Look, Alan, I have no interest in hanging
out with Mom's boyfriend du jour.&lt;/i>

05:40.619 --> 05:41.984
Why not? He seems like a great guy.

05:42.153 --> 05:43.677
He might be the greatest guy...

05:43.855 --> 05:47.222
...but he'll end up like every other husband
or boyfriend she's ever had.

05:47.392 --> 05:52.625
Either she'll dump him, he'll dump her,
or he'll die under suspicious circumstances.

05:53.231 --> 05:55.631
No matter what,
you're left standing on the curb...

05:55.800 --> 05:58.428
...with your fishing pole
on the first day of summer vacation...

05:58.603 --> 06:02.061
...waiting for a Chrysler LeBaron
that never comes.

06:04.509 --> 06:06.409
Okay, this isn't about Teddy, is it?

06:07.345 --> 06:10.576
Hey, hey. You wanna be buddies
with this guy, go right ahead.

06:10.749 --> 06:12.148
I've got better things to do.

06:12.317 --> 06:15.184
Better than ringside seats
to the Heavyweight Championship fight...

06:15.353 --> 06:17.480
...at Caesars Palace tomorrow night?

06:18.023 --> 06:19.513
What?

06:20.425 --> 06:21.892
Ringside.

06:22.494 --> 06:24.291
- Ringside?
- Any closer...

06:24.462 --> 06:26.657
...and we'd be sitting in the spit bucket.

06:28.266 --> 06:31.030
Should I call him back
and tell him you changed your mind?

06:32.003 --> 06:33.095
No, no. No.

06:33.271 --> 06:35.967
He's just using us to get closer to Mom.

06:36.141 --> 06:38.575
When we were kids
it was Disneyland and cotton candy.

06:38.743 --> 06:39.903
Now it's ringside seats.

06:40.078 --> 06:42.546
- And a private plane.
- He's got a private plane?

06:43.248 --> 06:46.547
And a limo and a penthouse suite.

06:46.718 --> 06:47.912
Oh.

06:49.220 --> 06:51.211
- Still not interested?
- No.

06:51.389 --> 06:53.857
- Still have better things to do?
- Yup.

06:54.025 --> 06:56.789
Ah. Do you realize what a stubborn child
you sound like?

06:56.962 --> 06:58.190
I do.

06:58.363 --> 07:01.127
- You're not gonna give it up, are you?
- Not a chance.

07:01.466 --> 07:04.333
Okay, then, good night.

07:04.602 --> 07:06.126
Good night.

07:22.053 --> 07:24.419
Oh, boy, Teddy's here.

07:24.589 --> 07:25.954
Charlie, Teddy's here.

07:26.591 --> 07:28.218
Oh, boy.

07:30.295 --> 07:32.286
Hi, Al, you all packed?

07:32.464 --> 07:34.432
Are you kidding? I packed last night.

07:34.599 --> 07:35.930
I was too excited to sleep.

07:36.501 --> 07:37.900
Terrific.

07:38.069 --> 07:40.560
- Where's Charlie?
- Out on the deck.

07:40.739 --> 07:42.866
- Give me a minute, I wanna say hi.
- All right.

07:43.041 --> 07:45.771
- Can I go sit in the limo?
- Knock yourself out.

07:45.944 --> 07:47.070
There's sushi.

07:47.245 --> 07:49.270
Sushi in a car. Oh, boy.

07:55.653 --> 07:57.848
This is your other plans?

07:58.023 --> 08:01.982
Not all of them. Later I'm gonna go inside
and watch some girl-on-girl porn.

08:03.061 --> 08:04.688
Beautiful.

08:05.930 --> 08:10.299
Look, I still have an extra ticket to the fight
and there's plenty of room on the plane.

08:10.468 --> 08:11.662
No, thanks.

08:12.170 --> 08:14.229
Did I do something to tick you off?

08:14.406 --> 08:17.102
You know,
aside from slipping it to your mother.

08:18.376 --> 08:21.937
No, no. It's just I'd prefer
not to get involved in her personal life.

08:22.113 --> 08:24.206
I'm not asking you to get involved
in her life.

08:24.382 --> 08:27.215
I'm asking you to come to vegas
with me and see a fight.

08:27.385 --> 08:28.784
Yeah, but why?

08:28.953 --> 08:31.285
I don't know, you seem like a nice guy.

08:31.856 --> 08:35.292
- Don't you have your own friends?
- Charlie, when you get to be my age...

08:35.460 --> 08:37.860
...most of your friends
are either married or dead.

08:38.630 --> 08:39.892
What's the difference?

08:40.532 --> 08:42.523
The dead ones smell up my plane.

08:44.769 --> 08:47.704
Come on, throw some clothes on
and let's go have some fun.

08:51.976 --> 08:53.773
Ah, what the hell.

08:53.945 --> 08:56.812
Just do me a favor.
Let's keep this between us.

08:57.315 --> 08:59.840
I want your mother to think
that I went on a business trip.

09:00.018 --> 09:03.749
No problem.
My mother still thinks I went to college.

09:04.956 --> 09:06.583
Beautiful.

09:14.732 --> 09:16.563
Hey, Charlie? You need anything?

09:16.868 --> 09:20.099
Teddy, if I was any happier,
my pants would be wet.

09:22.040 --> 09:24.304
Hey, Teddy, can we get some gelato
after the fight?

09:24.476 --> 09:25.738
Anything you want, kid.

09:25.910 --> 09:27.707
Gee, thanks.

09:33.351 --> 09:34.841
Hiya.

09:35.753 --> 09:37.243
What's up?

09:38.256 --> 09:41.350
Yeah. I've never really been a big fan
of the pugilistic arts...

09:41.526 --> 09:46.122
...but I have to admit, I'm getting kind of
swept away in the pageantry of the event.

09:46.965 --> 09:48.262
Uh-huh.

09:51.336 --> 09:53.566
I like your bling very much.

09:54.239 --> 09:58.403
I, uh, tried a pierced ear once,
but it got horribly infected.

10:01.513 --> 10:04.380
Hey, uh, you know
where we could score some good gelato?

10:05.150 --> 10:06.674
No.

10:09.821 --> 10:11.311
Word.

10:13.725 --> 10:15.716
I think that might be that Snoopy fella.

10:17.829 --> 10:18.887
Terrific.

10:23.101 --> 10:24.625
Hello?

10:24.936 --> 10:27.404
Oh, hi, Evelyn. Yeah.

10:27.572 --> 10:29.335
How are you, sweetheart?

10:29.507 --> 10:31.475
Good, good.

10:31.776 --> 10:32.800
Where am I?

10:34.879 --> 10:36.972
San Francisco.

10:38.449 --> 10:43.148
Uh, I'm going into a meeting, uh,
can I call you back?

10:43.488 --> 10:46.218
Love you too, sweetie. Love you.

10:47.425 --> 10:48.790
You're very good.

10:49.360 --> 10:50.884
Yeah.

10:51.596 --> 10:53.996
I've got 5 grand on the big Russian.

10:54.165 --> 10:57.464
Either of you fellas
like to have a piece of my action?

10:57.635 --> 10:59.796
- I'll take half.
- Attaboy.

10:59.971 --> 11:01.268
How about you, Alan?

11:01.906 --> 11:04.340
Aw, what the heck, I'm in vegas.
Heh-heh.

11:04.509 --> 11:05.771
Put me down for 20...

11:05.944 --> 11:07.844
No, $25.

11:10.949 --> 11:12.610
Make it 20.

11:18.723 --> 11:24.184
One. Two. Three. Four.

11:24.596 --> 11:27.793
- Five. Six.
- How do you say "get up" in Russian?

11:27.966 --> 11:30.594
Seven. Eight.

11:30.768 --> 11:33.202
Nine. Ten.

11:36.007 --> 11:37.338
Unbelievable.

11:37.508 --> 11:39.066
An 18-second fight.

11:39.811 --> 11:42.507
It takes me longer to start peeing.

11:43.448 --> 11:46.281
Yeah, thanks so much for giving me
half your action on the guy.

11:46.451 --> 11:48.578
No problem. You want the other half?

11:48.753 --> 11:49.742
No, I'm good.

11:51.222 --> 11:52.587
Oh, yeah, baby.

11:52.757 --> 11:55.555
Twenty dead presidents. I'm even.

11:57.395 --> 11:58.657
Was he a preemie?

11:59.264 --> 12:00.458
Actually, we both were.

12:00.632 --> 12:02.463
My mom waits nine months for nothing.

12:04.702 --> 12:07.694
Hey, fellas,
I wanna show you something.

12:08.072 --> 12:09.164
What do you think?

12:09.807 --> 12:11.741
- Nice.
- Yeah. Who's it for?

12:12.443 --> 12:15.173
- Your mother.
- No, seriously.

12:15.647 --> 12:18.912
I know it's kind of old-fashioned,
but I wanted to run it by you guys...

12:19.083 --> 12:20.607
...before I asked her.

12:20.785 --> 12:22.184
Ask her what?

12:22.587 --> 12:24.418
Charlie, I love your mom.

12:24.589 --> 12:25.783
I wanna marry her.

12:25.957 --> 12:30.587
But... But you could do so much better.

12:30.762 --> 12:32.662
That's no way to talk about your mother.

12:32.830 --> 12:35.162
That's precisely the way
to talk about my mother.

12:35.333 --> 12:36.664
Charlie, be supportive.

12:36.834 --> 12:38.426
I thought I was being supportive.

12:38.603 --> 12:42.869
Regardless of what you guys think
about her, Evelyn is a great broad.

12:43.041 --> 12:46.238
I wanna marry her
and I would like your blessing.

12:46.411 --> 12:49.574
- You've got my blessing, Teddy.
- Shut up and eat your gelato.

12:49.947 --> 12:52.279
Come on, Charlie, wouldn't it be great
to have a dad again?

12:52.617 --> 12:53.914
I'm a grown man, Alan.

12:54.085 --> 12:55.780
I don't need a father anymore.

12:56.654 --> 12:58.622
Would any of you gentlemen like a date?

12:58.790 --> 13:00.257
Sorry, doll, I'm taken.

13:00.425 --> 13:03.451
But I wouldn't mind footing the bill
for my two boys here.

13:03.895 --> 13:05.362
Hi, I'm Amber.

13:05.530 --> 13:06.656
I'm Tiffany.

13:09.667 --> 13:11.931
- Thanks, Daddy.
- Thanks, Daddy.

13:19.577 --> 13:21.772
- Hey.
- Hey.

13:22.347 --> 13:25.214
- What are you doing?
- Nothing. Nothing.

13:25.383 --> 13:26.941
How was work?

13:27.118 --> 13:28.881
You don't care about my work.

13:29.053 --> 13:32.022
- What's under the pillow?
- Hey, hey, hey.

13:33.758 --> 13:35.225
&lt;i>Modern Bride?&lt;/i>

13:36.928 --> 13:40.364
- I just read it for the articles.
- Really?

13:41.232 --> 13:45.168
Okay. I was looking for ideas
because I thought it would be nice...

13:45.336 --> 13:48.897
...if we had the wedding for Teddy
and Mom here in the house.

13:50.007 --> 13:51.668
Oh, my God.

13:53.911 --> 13:56.345
You're a mind reader.

13:57.115 --> 14:00.175
I didn't wanna bring it up,
because I was afraid you might say no.

14:00.351 --> 14:02.512
But I was up all night doing research.

14:02.687 --> 14:06.987
Now, I'm thinking a sunset ceremony with
the guests gathered on the beach below...

14:07.158 --> 14:11.390
...as the bride and groom cross onto the
deck wearing Polynesian wedding garb...

14:11.562 --> 14:14.895
...surrounded by tropical flowers
and tiki torches.

14:15.400 --> 14:17.561
Okay, what about it don't you like?

14:18.369 --> 14:20.599
Because I was a little iffy
on the tiki torches.

14:21.339 --> 14:24.467
You're a little iffy in so many ways.

14:24.876 --> 14:26.571
Okay, we can hammer out
the details later.

14:26.744 --> 14:30.111
The thing to remember
is we're doing this for someone we love.

14:30.281 --> 14:31.543
- Teddy.
- Teddy.

14:32.417 --> 14:33.782
Okay, I'm out of here.

14:33.951 --> 14:37.318
- Berta, did you hear the news about Mom?
- Yeah, she joined the Mormon Church...

14:37.488 --> 14:40.753
...so she can get a rent-controlled
apartment in Salt Lake City.

14:41.292 --> 14:42.725
Oh, you mean your mom. No.

14:45.296 --> 14:46.661
We're getting a new dad.

14:46.831 --> 14:49.095
- His name is Teddy.
- He took us to a boxing match.

14:49.267 --> 14:51.997
He bought us prostitutes and gelato.

14:52.670 --> 14:54.228
Well, congratulations.

14:54.405 --> 14:56.100
I'm real happy for you, boys.

14:56.274 --> 14:57.502
- Thanks.
- Thanks.

14:57.675 --> 15:00.610
I think my news was far more interesting.

15:00.978 --> 15:03.276
- I'm gonna call Teddy, tell him our plan.
- Oh, great.

15:03.448 --> 15:05.916
Ask him how he feels about tiki torches.

15:08.419 --> 15:11.786
- Hey, Teddy, it's Charlie.
- And Alan. Hi, Teddy.

15:11.956 --> 15:13.856
Yeah, Alan says hi.

15:14.025 --> 15:15.856
Listen, we've been thinking
about the wedding...

15:16.027 --> 15:17.858
Tiki torches.

15:19.297 --> 15:20.525
What?

15:20.698 --> 15:22.825
- You're kidding.
- What?

15:24.302 --> 15:26.702
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

15:29.407 --> 15:31.272
Wow. I don't believe it.

15:31.442 --> 15:33.706
- What?
- Mom turned him down.

15:33.878 --> 15:36.108
Ah! That bitch.

15:37.348 --> 15:41.682
Gee, Teddy, I don't know what to say.
L... I feel terrible.

15:41.853 --> 15:44.515
Well, this doesn't mean
we couldn't still hang out, right?

15:44.689 --> 15:45.781
So you'll call us?

15:45.957 --> 15:49.290
Great. Great, look forward to it.
All right. Bye-bye.

15:50.628 --> 15:53.563
I know that tone of voice.
We'll never hear from him.

15:54.565 --> 15:56.055
No tiki torches?

15:56.434 --> 15:58.698
I don't understand.
How could Mom say no to him?

15:58.870 --> 16:02.237
- He was perfect for her.
- Forget her. He was perfect for us.

16:03.274 --> 16:06.004
I'm closing the door to my heart, Charlie.

16:07.411 --> 16:09.003
It just hurts too much.

16:10.248 --> 16:12.808
Screw it, this isn't over. Come on.

16:13.451 --> 16:14.611
Where are we going?

16:14.785 --> 16:17.049
We are gonna talk some sense
into our mother.

16:17.221 --> 16:20.782
Really? It's hard to imagine
that turning out well.

16:23.861 --> 16:24.953
Mom?

16:25.129 --> 16:26.460
Mom, where the hell are you?

16:26.631 --> 16:28.656
- Maybe she's not home.
- She's home.

16:28.833 --> 16:31.165
Her car's in the driveway,
the alarm's not on. Mom!

16:31.602 --> 16:36.505
Boys, I gave you that key for emergencies,
not to barge in on me like the Gestapo.

16:38.543 --> 16:40.238
We wanna talk to you about Teddy.

16:40.411 --> 16:43.710
Teddy? Why in the world
would you wanna talk about Teddy?

16:43.881 --> 16:46.509
- Because we love Teddy.
- And you broke his heart.

16:47.752 --> 16:51.244
Hang on a second, you met the man
for five minutes in a coffee shop.

16:57.361 --> 16:59.955
Well, it was a good five minutes.

17:00.131 --> 17:02.725
Evelyn? Hey, what the hell's going on?

17:02.900 --> 17:04.595
I'll be right with you, sweetie.

17:04.769 --> 17:07.135
Look, this is not the best time.

17:07.505 --> 17:11.202
Come on, Evie,
the viagra's starting to make my ears burn.

17:14.011 --> 17:16.445
- Who are these clowns?
- Oh, Hugo, darling...

17:16.614 --> 17:19.378
...these are my sons, Charlie and Alan.

17:19.550 --> 17:21.677
Wait a minute,
you didn't tell me you had any kids.

17:21.852 --> 17:23.717
I sure didn't sign on for any kids.

17:23.888 --> 17:26.550
Just give me a minute, darling.
I'll be right with you.

17:26.958 --> 17:30.325
If I wanted to see any kids,
I'd go visit my own.

17:32.063 --> 17:33.291
How old are these nuts?

17:33.931 --> 17:35.831
From over here,
they look about a hundred.

17:38.169 --> 17:39.727
Mom, what about Teddy?

17:41.038 --> 17:44.735
Can we please have this conversation
another time?

17:44.909 --> 17:46.672
No, no. No, we are having it right now.

17:46.978 --> 17:48.377
What do you want me to say?

17:48.546 --> 17:50.878
Teddy's fine, I like Teddy.

17:51.048 --> 17:53.448
But he's ready to settle down
and I'm not.

17:53.618 --> 17:55.017
I want my freedom.

17:55.186 --> 17:59.122
Okay, I get freedom, but come on,
Teddy's way better than this guy.

17:59.290 --> 18:02.259
As I said, Teddy's fine...

18:02.426 --> 18:08.831
...but there are some areas in which
he just doesn't measure up to Hugo.

18:12.703 --> 18:14.898
- Oh, God!
- Oh, Mom!

18:16.507 --> 18:18.270
It's the biggest I've ever seen.

18:20.011 --> 18:22.946
Makes it won'th eating dinner at 3:30.

18:24.348 --> 18:27.317
- But... But Teddy...
- I don't wanna hear it.

18:27.485 --> 18:28.952
You have no say in this.

18:29.120 --> 18:32.248
This is my life,
and right now I don't wanna be tied down.

18:32.423 --> 18:33.412
I want options.

18:37.128 --> 18:38.288
Hugo?

18:42.400 --> 18:44.027
Hugo?

18:46.504 --> 18:49.632
Oh, God, no.
Quick, somebody give me the phone.

18:49.974 --> 18:51.566
Come on, come on.

18:51.842 --> 18:54.777
- Here, here, here.
- Oh, God.

18:56.714 --> 19:00.946
Come on, come on, come on.
Hello, Teddy?

19:04.121 --> 19:07.284
Oh, I'm so glad I caught you in.

19:11.762 --> 19:13.992
I hope you can forgive me, Teddy.

19:14.165 --> 19:16.599
I just needed time to think about it.

19:16.767 --> 19:21.136
It's like they say, "You don't know
what you've got till it's gone. "

19:21.439 --> 19:22.463
Yes.

19:23.107 --> 19:26.941
Yes, my darling, I love you too.

19:27.111 --> 19:29.443
Well, I'll be right over.

19:29.613 --> 19:31.137
Mwah.

19:35.953 --> 19:38.922
Could someone please
put a sheet over him?

19:40.024 --> 19:41.582
Mom, shouldn't we call 911?

19:41.926 --> 19:45.259
Well, call whoever you want,
the man is dead.

19:46.430 --> 19:48.762
You're really gonna leave
and go to Teddy's?

19:48.933 --> 19:52.425
Well, I can't very well
invite him over here.

19:54.872 --> 19:57.272
All right. She's going back to Teddy.

19:57.441 --> 20:00.103
Hey, hey, hey, a little respect?

20:00.277 --> 20:01.972
Oh... oh, yeah.

20:04.548 --> 20:06.709
- Okay. Who's our daddy?
- Teddy!

20:06.884 --> 20:08.351
Right.
